id: 10
hanzi: 灾害
pinyin: zāi hài
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: disaster; calamity; catastrophe; devastation
  es: desastre; calamidad; catástrofe; siniestro

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | an event causing extensive damage, suffering, or loss of life, resulting from natural forces or human action | desastre; calamidad; catástrofe natural o humana que provoca grandes estragos y pérdidas | 自然灾害 (natural disaster)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 古代民间将年兽视为象征严冬与饥荒的凶残灾害，唯有全村老幼齐心协力方能化险为夷。 | Gǔdài mínjiān jiāng Niánshòu shìwéi xiàngzhēng yándōng yǔ jīhuāng de xiōngcán zāihài, wéiyǒu quáncūn lǎoyòu qíxīn-xiélì fāng néng huàxiǎn-wéiyí. | Ancient folk regarded the beast Nian as a vicious disaster symbolizing harsh winter and famine, which could only be overcome if all villagers united as one. | En el folclore antiguo se consideraba a la fiera Nian una calamidad feroz que personificaba el crudo invierno y el hambre, superable solo con la unión comunitaria.
  #2 | 健全的防灾减灾救灾体制能够在气象灾害来临前迅速启动预警，从而最大程度减少人员伤亡和财产损失。 | Jiànquán de fángzāi jiǎnzāi jiùzāi tǐzhì nénggòu zài qìxiàng zāihài láilín qián xùnsù qǐdòng yùjǐng, cóng'ér zuìdà chéngdù jiǎnshǎo rényuán shāngwáng hé cáichǎn sǔnshī. | A well-developed disaster prevention, mitigation, and relief mechanism can promptly trigger early warnings before meteorological disasters strike, thereby minimizing casualties and property loss. | Un sistema integral de prevención y socorro permite activar alertas inmediatas ante desastres meteorológicos, reduciendo al máximo víctimas humanas y pérdidas materiales.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  自然灾害 | natural disaster
  地质灾害 | geological hazard / disaster
  气象灾害 | meteorological disaster
  遭受灾害 | suffer a disaster
  防灾减灾 | disaster prevention and mitigation
  抵御灾害 | resist / withstand disasters

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  救灾恤患 | jiù zāi xù huàn | relieve victims of disaster and pity the distressed
  祸起萧墙 | huò qǐ xiāo qiáng | trouble arises within the home walls; internal strife
  降灾降福 | jiàng zāi jiàng fú | bestow blessings or send down calamities
  多灾多难 | duō zāi duō nàn | plagued with frequent disasters and misfortunes

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  灾 | zāi | disaster; calamity; catastrophe | desastre; calamidad; siniestro; fuego destructor | 宀 | roof / house | 宀 (house roof) + 火 (fire burning inside) | "" | 7 | 上下结构 | Ideogrammic compound of fire (火) blazing uncontrollably beneath a domestic roof (宀), graphically portraying an internal house fire disaster. | Fire flames (火) erupting through the roof of a house (宀), illustrating a destructive household calamity. | Llamas devoradoras (火) que brotan del techo de una casa (宀), simbolizando un desastre destructivo. | 55 | JCF | 災
  害 | hài | harm; injure; damage; evil | dañar; mal; perjuicio; plaga | 宀 | roof with chimney | 宀 (protective residential roof) | 丯 (harmful words / obstruction) + 口 (mouth) | 10 | 上下结构 | Ideogrammic compound where harmful words (丯) uttered from the mouth (口) beneath the roof (宀) inflict internal destruction. | Bitter words from a mouth (口) under the house roof (宀) causing discord and grave harm. | Palabras enconadas de una boca (口) bajo el techo hogareño (宀) que desatan discordia y perjuicio familiar. | 51 | JTMK | ""

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: A destructive fire under the roof (灾) that brings severe harm to the household (害) constitutes a devastating disaster (灾害).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Un fuego devorador bajo el tejado (灾) que inflige grave perjuicio al hogar (害) desata un temible desastre (灾害).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Ancient agricultural civilization in China constantly battled nature's unpredictability (flood, drought, locusts, and harsh winter freezes). Mythological creatures like Nian were personified embodiments of environmental calamities (灾害). Rituals of red banners, noise, and sleepless watch (守岁) unified the community against seasonal catastrophes.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High level 1st tone 'zāi' (55) plunging directly into falling 4th tone 'hài' (51). Clear contrast from sustained high pitch to abrupt descent.

