    患 | huàn | disaster; trouble; worry

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 灾害 specifically denotes wide-scale physical, meteorological, or social catastrophes causing broad devastation to populations or environments.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 灾害 vs. 灾难 | zāinàn | 灾害 highlights the objective physical destruction and material devastation caused by events (e.g. 地质灾害, 农业灾害), whereas 灾难 emphasizes the tragic human suffering, emotional grief, and personal misery experienced by victims.
    2 | 灾害 vs. 事故 | shìgù | 灾害 encompasses broad natural or large-scale calamities (floods, blizzards, plagues), whereas 事故 denotes localized, often man-made operational failures, mishaps, or accidents in transport and industry (e.g. 交通事故, 生产事故).
    3 | 灾害 vs. 危害 | wēihài | 灾害 is a concrete event or phenomenon of devastation (a noun), whereas 危害 is an ongoing harmful action or detrimental potential that undermines health, safety, or society (often functioning as a transitive verb).

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在远古先民的记忆中，严冬与匮乏本身就是莫大的灾害。年兽下山的传说，本质上是对自然破坏力的恐惧投射。除夕夜的灯火与锣鼓，是人类在灾害面前用团结筑起的心灵防线。 | Zài yuǎngǔ xiānmín de jìyì zhōng, yándōng yǔ kuìfá běnshēn jiùshì mòdà de zāihài. Niánshòu xiàshān de chuánshuō, běnzhì shàng shì duì zìrán pòhuàilì de kǒngjù tóushè. Chúxī yè de dēnghuǒ yǔ luógǔ, shì rénlèi zài zāihài miànqián yòng tuánjié zhùqǐ de xīnlíng fángxiàn. | In the collective memories of ancient ancestors, harsh winter and scarcity were immense disasters in themselves. The legend of the beast Nian descending was fundamentally a projection of fear toward nature's destructive power. The lanterns and gongs on New Year's Eve represented a spiritual defense line built through solidarity against disasters. | En la memoria de los antepasados, el crudo invierno y la carestía eran grandes calamidades. La leyenda de la fiera Nian reflejaba el terror ante las fuerzas ciegas de la naturaleza. Las luces y tambores de fin de año levantaron una barrera espiritual forjada en la unión humana frente al desastre.
  #2 | 面对日益频发的极端气候与地质灾害，构建智慧韧性城市已成为可持续发展的战略重心。通过遥感监测与大数据预警，现代应急体系能够在灾害初起时精准研判，全面守护人民生命财产安全。 | Miànduì rìyì pínfā de jíduān qìhòu yǔ dìzhì zāihài, gòujiàn zhìhuì rènxìng chéngshì yǐ chéngwéi kěchíxù fāzhǎn de zhànlüè zhòngxīn. Tōngguò yáogǎn jiāncè yǔ dàshùjù yùjǐng, xiàndài yìngjí tǐxì nénggòu zài zāihài chūqǐ shí jīngzhǔn yánpàn, quánmiàn shǒuhù rénmín shēngmìng cáichǎn ānquán. | In the face of increasingly frequent extreme climate and geological disasters, constructing smart, resilient cities has become a strategic priority for sustainable development. Through remote sensing and big data warnings, modern emergency systems can analyze threats precisely at the onset of disasters, comprehensively safeguarding citizens' lives and assets. | Ante desastres meteorológicos y geológicos cada vez más frecuentes, crear urbes inteligentes y resilientes es una prioridad estratégica. Con sensores remotos y modelos de datos, los sistemas modernos de emergencia predicen catástrofes con precisión, salvaguardando vidas y bienes.